### Technical Context

**Application Architecture:**
- Backend Services: Domain-aligned microservices (Claims API, Eligibility API, Provider API)
- Backend Events: EventBridge publishes domain events (claim.adjudicated, provider.credentialed)
- Micro-Frontends: 6-10 independently deployed modules
- API Gateway: Single entry point for all backend APIs

**Current State (Frontend State Management):**

```typescript
// ❌ PROBLEM: Claims module caches claim data in frontend state

// claims-mfe/src/pages/ClaimsList.tsx
function ClaimsList() {
  const [claims, setClaims] = useState<Claim[]>([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    // Fetch claims on mount
    fetch('/api/claims')
      .then((res) => res.json())
      .then((data) => {
        setClaims(data.claims);
        setLoading(false);
      });
  }, []);

  // User opens Claim Detail page, navigates back to Claims List
  // Claims List shows stale data (doesn't refetch)

  return (
    <ul>
      {claims.map((claim) => (
        <li key={claim.id}>
          {claim.claimNumber} - {claim.status}  {/* Stale status! */}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}
```

**Problems:**
1. Claims List shows stale data after user returns from Claim Detail (no refetch)
2. User sees "Pending" status but backend already updated to "Approved"
3. No cache invalidation strategy (data stays stale until page refresh)
4. No optimistic updates (user waits for backend response)

