[patterns/application/micro-frontend/PTN-APP-MFE-012-backend-api-integration-pattern.md#variation-3-prefetching-on-hover]

#### Variation 3: Prefetching on Hover

Prefetch claim details when user hovers over claim item (perceived performance).

**When to Use:**
- Detail pages likely to be visited after list view
- Improve perceived performance (instant navigation)
- Reduce time-to-interactive

**Implementation:**

```typescript
// claims-mfe/src/components/ClaimItem.tsx
import { useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query';

function ClaimItem({ claim }) {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();

  const prefetchClaimDetail = () => {
    queryClient.prefetchQuery({
      queryKey: ['claim', claim.id],
      queryFn: () => claimsAPIClient.getClaim(claim.id),
      staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // Cache for 5 minutes
    });
  };

  return (
    <Link
      to={`/claims/${claim.id}`}
      onMouseEnter={prefetchClaimDetail}  // Prefetch on hover
      onFocus={prefetchClaimDetail}        // Prefetch on keyboard focus (a11y)
    >
      {claim.claimNumber} - {claim.status}
    </Link>
  );
}
```

**Benefits:**
- **Instant Navigation**: Detail page loads instantly (data already cached)
- **Better UX**: No loading spinner on navigation
- **Smart Prefetching**: Only prefetch on hover (not all items upfront)

**Trade-offs:**
- **Unnecessary Requests**: User may hover without clicking (wasted bandwidth)
- **Cache Churn**: Prefetched data expires if user doesn't navigate

